msgctxt "ui"
msgid "Bandwidth target Mbps"
msgstr ""

#: ui/app.slint:877
msgctxt "ui"
msgid ""
"Adaptive bitrate is the default. A manual ceiling requests your chosen Mbps "
"from the Mac; static screens and encoder limits can lower the actual rate, "
"and bursts may exceed it. Compression, JPEG quality and the VNC bandwidth "
"target do not apply. Apply reconnects when changing transports, HEVC presets "
"or the bitrate ceiling; saved logins require Windows Hello again."
msgstr ""

#: ui/app.slint:877
msgctxt "ui"
msgid ""
"Automatic means no bandwidth target. A manual target spaces screen requests "
"based on received bytes; bursts can exceed it. Apply reconnects "
"automatically when switching to or from HEVC. Other VNC changes apply live."
msgstr ""

#: ui/app.slint:879
msgctxt "ui"
msgid "Frame rate limit"
msgstr ""

#: ui/app.slint:880
msgctxt "ui"
msgid "Maximum FPS"
msgstr ""

#: ui/app.slint:882
msgctxt "ui"
msgid "Show live FPS counter"
msgstr ""

#: ui/app.slint:883
msgctxt "ui"
msgid ""
"FPS counts unique desktop images submitted for display, not monitor "
"refreshes. An idle desktop correctly reads 0 FPS. Traffic measures VNC, HEVC/"
"audio SRTP and SSH payloads in bits/s, excluding TCP/UDP/VPN overhead."
msgstr ""

#: ui/app.slint:901
msgctxt "ui"
msgid ""
"Standard VNC offers CopyRect and a Raw fallback; the Mac may ignore "
"compression/JPEG hints. HEVC uses Apple's separate High Performance "
"transport with encrypted control, SRTP video and optional audio. Video "
"decoding is bundled; audio uses a separate converter. Mac account login and "
"UDP on the VNC port and the next port are required. H.264 playback is not "
"supported."
msgstr ""

